# Intake workflow (paste a case → generated spec; user runs it manually)

Follow this whenever the user pastes or describes a manual test case (any format, even rough). Do not ask where files go. Process several cases **one at a time**.

Read and obey `.cursor/rules/framework-rules.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/manual-testcase-template.mdc`. After generation, apply `.cursor/rules/review-checklist.mdc`.

**Execution boundary:** Generate and review code only. The user always runs Playwright tests manually. Never invoke a test runner, including through npm scripts.

## Steps (do all of them)

1. **Normalise and save the case.** Use the template. Path: `docs/manual-test-cases/TC-NNN-<kebab-title>.md` where NNN is the next free number (`TC-001` if none exist). Set `Status: Ready`. If something is ambiguous, make a reasonable assumption, **state it**, and continue. Ask only if truly blocked (missing credential that cannot be generated, unknown product that the live site does not have).
2. **Classify** as UI, API, or Hybrid. Spec lives in `tests/ui/`, `tests/api/`, or `tests/hybrid/` respectively. One TC per spec file.
3. **Inventory** existing page objects, API methods, fixtures, factories, utils, and constants. List gaps before writing code.
4. **Verify on the live site** any locator, message text, URL path, or endpoint you do not already have in the repo. Use Playwright codegen, the browser tool, or a documented API call. **Never invent.**
5. **Close gaps** in pages, API clients, fixtures, data factories, and utils. Follow framework-rules. Do not put selectors or URLs in specs.
6. **Write the spec.** Import `test, expect` from `src/fixtures`. Title: `'Type | Description | TC-NNN'`. Tags via `{ tag: [...] }`. `test.step` per manual step group. `expect` per expected result. At least two meaningful assertions.
7. **Static quality checks only; do not execute tests.** Never run `npx playwright test`, `npm test`, `npm run test`, or any command/script that starts the Playwright test runner. Do not run the generated spec, the full suite, retries, or `--repeat-each`. You may run `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` only if you have confirmed those scripts perform static checks and do not trigger tests. Report checks that were not run as `Not run`—never imply they passed.
8. **Update docs.** Case file: `Automated: Yes` when the spec has been generated, `Spec:` path, and keep `Status: Ready` pending the user's manual execution. Add/update the traceability row in `docs/manual-test-cases/README.md`. Append mistakes and fixes to `docs/ai-review-log.md`. Change status to `Automated` only after the user confirms a successful manual run.
9. **Reply** with a short summary: files created/changed, assumptions, static-check results, and the exact command the user can run manually. Explicitly state: `Playwright tests were not executed by the AI; awaiting your manual run.` Do not report pass/fail counts unless the user supplied actual execution results.

## Manual execution handoff

After code generation, provide the exact command for the user, for example:

```bash
npx playwright test tests/ui/tc-NNN-example.spec.ts --project=chromium
```

The command is guidance only; do not execute it. The user owns all test execution and result confirmation. Until confirmation, leave the case `Ready` and describe the automation as generated but not yet execution-verified.

## Out of scope

Do not start this workflow for unrelated questions (how to run tests, config tweaks) unless a case is being added or changed.
